  "question": {
    "text": "A capacitor of reactance $4 \\sqrt{3} \\Omega$ and a resistor of resistance $4 \\Omega$ are connected in series with an ac source of peak value $8 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~V}$. The power dissipation in the circuit is ________ W.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/weRLsccgGbZHC9B_vLEHiqIRr7IfZe7_HwftrYH0nM8.original.fullsize.png\"/>\n$\\begin{aligned} &amp; \\mathrm{Z}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{R}^2+\\mathrm{X}^2 \\mathrm{~L}} \\\\ &amp; \\mathrm{Z}=\\sqrt{4^2+(4 \\sqrt{3})^2}=8 \\Omega \\\\ &amp; \\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{rms}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{V}}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{8 \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}=(8 \\mathrm{~V}) \\\\ &amp; \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{rms}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{rms}}}{\\mathrm{Z}}=\\frac{8}{8}=1 \\mathrm{~A}\\end{aligned}$\nPower dissipated $=\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{rms}}^2 \\times \\mathrm{R}=1 \\times 4=(4 \\mathrm{~W})$",
    "image": null
  },
